/P 102 0 R
/E (The Dorian mode is very often  accompanied by a pendulum movement that goes from the i chord to the IV chord \(Cm to F in the figure above\). The choice of chords is based on the idea of highlighting the "special note" of each chord. I wrote them as open triads, as those sound much better than closed triads. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
